2026-11-06T03:01:14.1979569Z 
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1980498Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1981988Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1982661Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1983417Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1983660Z 
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1983883Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1984250Z 
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1984507Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1985086Z    can use Nix.
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1985268Z 
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1985423Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1985636Z 
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1986047Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1986750Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1987640Z 
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1987807Z I will:
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1988021Z 
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1988258Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1988809Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1989386Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1989930Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1990508Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1990881Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1991355Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-11-06T03:01:14.1993128Z    /root
2026-11-06T03:01:14.2023915Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-11-06T03:01:14.2024601Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-11-06T03:01:14.2034506Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-11-06T03:01:14.2034945Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
